---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import framework from "../../content/framework/draft.json";

const responseCount = new Map(framework.challenges.map((challenge) => [challenge.id, framework.responses.filter(({ challengeId }) => challengeId === challenge.id).length]));
---
<BaseLayout fullBleed description="Explore recurring political-economic Challenges, institutional responses, and the evidence still needed to evaluate them.">
  <header class="framework-hero">
    <p class="coordinate">ENDS AND MEANS / RESEARCH DRAFT</p>
    <div><h1>Start with the question.<br /><span>Trace what follows.</span></h1><p class="dek">Political and economic traditions pursue different Ends through different institutional Means. Begin with a shared Challenge, then inspect the proposed mechanisms, failure hypotheses, and research gaps.</p></div>
    <aside class="draft-notice"><strong>Working material</strong><p>The current comparison has been reorganized, not certified. Its inherited claims remain visible as research leads until they receive claim-level sources and bounded cases.</p><a href="/framework/">How to read this draft →</a></aside>
  </header>
  <nav aria-label="Explore by Topic"><p class="coordinate">EXPLORE BY TOPIC</p><ul class="topic-strip">{framework.topics.map((topic) => <li><a href={`/topics/${topic.id}/`}>{topic.label}</a></li>)}</ul></nav>
  <section class="question-ledger" aria-labelledby="questions-title">
    <header class="section-heading"><div><p class="coordinate">DISCOVERY / 9 OPEN QUESTIONS</p><h2 id="questions-title">Choose a Challenge</h2></div><p>Each question opens the same analytical structure across multiple traditions.</p></header>
    <ol>{framework.challenges.map((challenge, index) => <li><a href={`/challenges/${challenge.id}/`}><span class="ledger-index">{String(index + 1).padStart(2, "0")}</span><span class="ledger-question">{challenge.question}</span><span class="ledger-count">{responseCount.get(challenge.id)} draft responses</span><span class="ledger-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></li>)}</ol>
  </section>
  <section class="framework-directory" aria-labelledby="traditions-title">
    <div><p class="coordinate">ANOTHER ENTRY POINT</p><h2 id="traditions-title">Explore traditions and ideal types</h2><p>These are contested families of ideas, not labels for whole countries or uniform blueprints.</p></div>
    <ul class="text-directory">{framework.traditions.map((tradition) => <li><a href={`/traditions/${tradition.id}/`}>{tradition.name}<span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></li>)}</ul>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
